      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-0828/cat-harness/process/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns/Process",
      "name": "Multi-locale translation",
      "summary": "Translate one or more layers into several locales at once, as a team: one source-language lead, one translator per locale, an untainted round trip, and the owner's merge window.",
      "description": "Translate one or more layers into several locales at once, as a team: one source-language lead, one translator per locale, an untainted round trip, and the owner's merge window. The result is unofficial, on main, and kept current by a watcher.\n\nYou are in this process when more than one locale is being produced from the same source at the same time. `translation-workflow` is the machine half for one catalogue and `human-translation-workflow` is the path to an official, signed-off translation; this process is the team around them. It extracts ONCE: every locale starts from the same templates, merged to main in one source PR before any locale begins, and no translator re-extracts. Each locale then lands as its own PR to main, never into the source branch, and a source PR's branch receives nothing after it merges.\n\nTwo things are never done in a translation: fixing the source (a source-text error is reported as one issue to the lead), and editing a FHIR resource inline (terms go into one CodeSystem supplement per locale). Officiality is not decided here: every catalogue is written unofficial, and a person makes it official through human-translation-workflow.",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "sourcePath": "library/processes/multi-locale-translation.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/library/processes/multi-locale-translation.bpmn",
